      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name recalls the Catawba people, the indigenous tribe that once inhabited the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catawba%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic Murray’s Mill and the Bunker Hill Covered Bridge stand as reminders of the region’s craftsmanship and heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://catawba-nc.b-cdn.net/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Catawba Historic District, Alexander Moore Farm, Murray's Mill Historic District, and Powell–Trollinger Lime Kilns are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catawba%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
